  "description": "Run NovaCredit, a new digital lender, and decide who gets which of four credit cards to earn the most profit. The catch: the safest customers aren't the most profitable, and good data isn't free. Start with a basic dataset and a fixed budget, cross profit thresholds to unlock exclusive data packs, and outbid rival teams before the data is gone. Judging Criteria: Winners are decided by a published scoring formula and a panel of judges, so every result can be checked. Scoring considers: Portfolio Profit : How much your card decisions earn on a hidden set of applicants nobody sees until the end. Smart Spending : How little of your budget you needed to get there. Memo : How well you justify your data purchases, and whether your lending is fair and responsible. The final reveal shows which data packs were treasure, which were traps, and who overpaid. REGISTRSTION IS FREE!! Format: Round 1: Online Preliminary Qualifier A 30 minutes multiple choice questions challenge hosted on Unstop. Questions in this round will be from basic mathematics and statistics with a few machine learning algorithmic concepts . Top 25 teams will advance to the on-campus Grand Finale . Round 2: On-Campus Grand Finale A high-intensity 3 -hour onsite showdown with hidden evaluation test cases. Submission will be closed by the end of the 3 hour mark. Participants must bring their own laptops Rules: Team Size : 2 –4 members. Duration : 3 hours. Participation : Open to all college/university students of any major. Tools : Python on your own laptop. No GPU needed; any library or AI assistant is allowed. Kaggle account mandartory for atleast one memeber of the team . Deliverables : A card decision for every applicant, the notebook that produced it, and a one-page memo explaining your data purchases and lending choices.",
